  "content_md": "Hmmmmmm\n\n![[5gaytep72qsves6nj8t4ngk7tp]]\n\n",
  "content_html": "<p>Hmmmmmm</p>\n\n<blockquote class=\"blyg-transclusion\" data-blyg-id=\"5gaytep72qsves6nj8t4ngk7tp\" data-blyg-version=\"1\" data-blyg-origin=\"https://www.msweet.net/notes/\">\n<p>It’s handy to have a default way to signal, to yourself and others, that you think <em>something</em> about X but aren’t sure what. “Hmmm” is becoming that for me. This yields a surprising boon to the economics of noticing: it lowers the bar for what gets registered. More things snag, without a matching rise in the energy it takes to capture them.</p>\n</blockquote>\n",
